                      deterministic,return_errors]

===========================================================================================
1. CODE SIZE
Chunk byte counts are chunk PAYLOAD (beam_lib), excluding the 8-byte chunk
header and 4-byte padding. Because the paired modules are identical apart
from the guard, the Code delta is the function's own bytecode delta exactly.
`instrs` counts symbolic BEAM instructions in the function under test only
(beam_disasm), which is attributable by construction. ImpT is the imported
MFA table -- a guard that proves a term's shape lets a CHECKED bif be
replaced by an UNCHECKED instruction, dropping the import, which shows here.

